{
  "seed": 1,
  "notes": "One DataSF footprint on the Grant/Clay corner that carries two street buildings. South 40% (the Clay corner): grey scored stucco with a deep cream marquee canopy wrapping onto Clay, roller shutters and small shops, fire escape on the Clay face. North 60%: white smooth stucco, ground + 3 storeys of regular punched wood windows, a steel fire escape, a continuous brown canopy over packed souvenir shopfronts with scissor gates and an arched lobby door. Height and storeys from LiDAR + roll (the corner part reads taller on the street; known gap). The corner part gets its deep cream boxed marquee canopy wrapping onto Clay (marqueeSpans, replaces the canvas awning there), a red clay-tile pent eave along its top on both faces with two stepped cream parapet gables on the Grant face (eaveSpans, gables), and a balustraded balcony belt under the top storey (balustradeSpans), and the Clay-face fire escape (sideFireEscapes; the base builder draws the front one only). The white part's continuous canopy becomes a deep brown sheet marquee with a scalloped white valance and soffit lamps (marqueeSpans + canopyValance) instead of a thin awning; every shop window and open scissor gate gets tiered stands packed with colourful stock behind the glass (windowDisplays); the stair lobby door gets its cream plaster arch surround (archBays); gold vertical trim strips at the corner and on the party line between the two street buildings (cornerPilasters); upper windows get warm room backing and part-drawn cream blinds (glassBacking). Stock, brown canopy and shutters rendered near-black because a `@tint` multiplies the kit base and painted-steel is #2b3236 - stock and canopy now multiply painted-white; the two full-bay slatted gates on Grant become open stocked shopfronts with folded scissor gates at their jambs and hanging merchandise. Clay-face and corner shutters are grey horizontal roll-ups (painted-steel-light); the corner marquee reads gold/cream with stepped cornice, gilt beads and rosettes (marqueeTrim); the canopy valance is a fine fringe; the lobby arch is 24-segment with an outer moulding ring; scored joints on the grey corner part; upper windows drop the opaque backing planes for side drapes, sill furniture and pictures (windowDressing); gondola shelving inside the shops (shopGondolas). Typeset sign lettering (Blender built-in DejaVu Sans and bundled Noto Sans CJK, both free licences; generic trade words only), deeper brown Grant canopy with finer valance, muted stock, slim arch, Clay shopfront, lanterns, AC units, grime. The corner part's crown - deeper red clay-tile pent eave on both faces with gold brackets, larger cream scrolled gables, a recessed dark loggia storey with columns behind the balustrade on Grant, and a 0.3 m parapet step (the LiDAR median 15.73 m caps the shell; the footprint's LiDAR peak 21.74 m supports a taller corner that the single-height gate cannot express). White part: paired window groups (7 per storey), one fire escape near 0.72 with a drop ladder, the extra corner-block Grant escape removed, fewer AC units. Coffered ribs on the cream marquee, two projecting blade signs. The corner part repainted pale cream-grey stucco with faint scoring (was reading brown/brick), lighter grime; its crown becomes a tall steep red clay-tile pent roof from the parapet top (1.35 m drop) over a second bracketed tile tier, larger scrolled cream gables standing proud of the tiles, terracotta coping on the parapet step; the white part whiter; the marquee cream/gold instead of saturated yellow; two raised skylight monitors and a few roof units on the deck; upper floors furnished as residential flats (bed, sofa, dresser) instead of the office kit. The red clay-tile pent over the corner part is 2.3 m tall (was 1.35) with its bracket tier moved under it, the cream parapet gables are 25% wider and rise from 2.9 m below the top to the LiDAR +0.5 m cap, and three shop boards take green, cream and blue grounds so the frontage is not one repeated yellow placard. The corner part still cannot stand taller than the white part: the height gate caps every part at the footprint's LiDAR median + 0.5 m. north 60% neutral painted-white (was painted-stucco whose warm kit base read tan/brown), corner part pale grey painted-white@dedede with the scored lines; tone step at 0.40 marks the two buildings. gold corner marquee with rafter soffit, bracketed gold balcony soffits, red corner crests, dark-brown fascia and deeper valance on the white canopy, roll-up shutters and grey scored wall on Clay, dark sash frames, lace curtains, more AC units, goods and grilles, white fire escapes, dark recessed lobby arch.",
